{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>But Luz was the name of the city at first.</b> The place that he called Beit-El is Jerusalem. What need was there to inform us that it was called Luz at first, and what benefit reaches us from this? It may be said that Scripture comes to hint to us through this name that from here the world began to be perfected and renewed — behold, it is the beginning of creation and renewal. Therefore He revealed to us that the name of the city at first was Luz, from the term לוז — the Luz of the spine in a person, from which he is destined to shake himself awake and be renewed and healed for the resurrection of the dead. For just as the wonder of renewal came from there, so too the wonder of the resurrection of the dead will begin from there. And David the king, peace be upon him, already explained this matter and said that the creation of the earth, and likewise the creation of the soul and the body — all is from the central one, which is Zion. And this is what he said (Psalms 50:1): ״אל אלהים ה' דבר ויקרא ארץ״, (ibid.) ״מציון מכלל יופי״, (ibid.) ״יקרא אל השמים מעל״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:56.157747614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}